The pmfcmd and pmfzmat files have been set up such that the C-C
distance goes from 2.0 to 3.0 A as lambda goes from 0 to 1. Any
subsequent change in lambda is then the same change in Angstroms,
e.g., delta lambda = 0.1 yields a change of 0.1 Angstrom. The pmfcmd
file is set up such that the chosen lambda values are to be added to
the lambda=0 value (2.0 A) to yield the CC separation. Thus, the
d350 job is run at CC = 3.50 A with perturbations to 3.40 and 3.60 A;
it uses lambda0,1 and 2 values of 1.500, 1.400, and 1.600, as indicated
below.
